    "explanation": "$(2n + 1)^2 = 4n^2 + 4n + 1$ and $(2n - 1)^2 = 4n^2 - 4n + 1$. Their difference is $8n$, a multiple of 8. For 51 and 49, $2n + 1 = 51$ gives $n = 25$, so $51^2 - 49^2 = 8 \\times 25 = 200$.",
    "workedSolution": "**(a)** $(2n + 1)(2n + 1) = 4n^2 + 2n + 2n + 1 = 4n^2 + 4n + 1$.\n\n**(b)** $(2n - 1)^2 = 4n^2 - 4n + 1$. Difference: $4n^2 + 4n + 1 - 4n^2 + 4n - 1 = 8n$, which is $8 \\times$ an integer.\n\n**(c)** $51 = 2n + 1$ when $n = 25$, so $51^2 - 49^2 = 8 \\times 25 = 200$. (Check: $2601 - 2401 = 200$.)",
    "hints": [
      "Expand both squares, then subtract with brackets.",
      "A number of the form $8 \\times (\\text{integer})$ is a multiple of 8."
    ],
